            "text": "In *Call of Duty*, eliminating opponents depends on the game mode, your weapon loadout, and your platform (PC, PlayStation, Xbox, or Mobile). Here are the primary ways to eliminate an enemy player:\n\n### 1. Shooting (Guns)\n* **Aim Down Sights (ADS):** Hold the aim button (**Right Mouse Click** on PC, **L2** on PlayStation, **LT** on Xbox) to look through your weapon's sights for better accuracy.\n* **Fire:** Press or hold the attack button (**Left Mouse Click** on PC, **R2** on PlayStation, **RT** on Xbox).\n* **Headshots:** Aim for the head or upper chest to deal significantly more damage and secure faster eliminations.\n\n### 2. Melee Attacks\n* **Basic Melee:** When close to an opponent, press the melee button (**E** or **V** on PC, **R3 / Right Stick Click** on console) to strike them with your weapon or fist. \n* **Finishing Moves (Executions):** Sneak up directly behind an enemy and **hold down the melee button**. This triggers a cinematic takedown that instantly eliminates the player, even if they have full armor.\n\n### 3. Equipment (Lethals)\n* Throw lethal equipment using the lethal button (**G** on PC, **R1** on PlayStation, **RB** on Xbox):\n  * **Frag Grenades / Semtex:** Explosives that deal heavy area damage.\n  * **Throwing Knives / Combat Axes:** Instant one-hit kills if they hit the target directly.\n  * **Claymores / Proximity Mines:** Place these near doorways or high-traffic areas to catch flanking enemies.\n\n### 4. Killstreaks / Scorestreaks\n* Earning a specific number of kills or score without dying unlocks powerful support tools (like UAVs, Cruise Missiles, Precision Airstrikes, or Chopper Gunners) that can eliminate multiple enemies across the map.\n\n### General Tips for Success:\n* **Check the Mini-Map:** Keep an eye on red dots indicating unsuppressed gunfire.\n* **Manage Recoil:** Pull your aim slightly downward while firing automatic weapons to counteract the gun's upward kick.\n* **Use Cover:** Avoid running in the open; move between walls, obstacles, and buildings to make yourself a harder target.",
